ecially a couple years ago a little  email what do you have to say about this  any thoughts  which is a dream come true when you get  a query and  i would say look you won't want it  because i'm kind of a curmudgeon on this  and  i wish we had a  neutral  reserve asset like goal something  universally recognized something that's  had constant purchasing power over  centuries  i mean this is crazy you you don't want  to put this as a lead op-ed on the  nation's premier business  newspaper  and he would write back yep sounds great  write it up  and and so i've had a chance um i don't  just  some people call me a gold bug but it's  not really that what i'm saying is  money is a tool it's not something  that's descended from heaven and yet we  live under legal tender laws of mandated  money you have to use  the dollar and i think that  implies  a moral contract on the part of  government if they're going to be the  producers of the dollar they better make  it a good product  to be a good product it has to fulfill  those functions of medium of exchange  unit of account and a store of value and  it has to do it honestly and with  reliability and with integrity do they  pay you to do that  or the journal yeah  i think it's gone over the years from  150 dollars  to  the one they ran a week or so ago i got  604 so  you could not make a living i asked you  for how many words  um usually 1200.  i want to go back in history again  because you had this  i don't know what you call this  relationship with russia back then and  um  with the wall coming down and  20 years of russia after let's let's  listen to what you had to say  i've always liked the literature tolstoy  and dostoevsky  and pushkin and goggle and  what i'm trying to do now is um  i'm trying to memorize  a day in the life of ivan de nisovich by  nitsan  so i i have tapes  of solzhenitsyn reciting his work  and then i have a russian russian or  english in russian  and then i have the work in russian and  i have it in